  "final_answer": "I searched Booking.com for Jan 3–6, 2027 (3 nights, 2 adults, prices in SGD) and filtered to properties within 1 km of the National University of Singapore. Only three hotels are that close, and all three come in well under your S$500 budget:\n\n1. **Fragrance Hotel – Ocean View** (Queenstown) — 1 km from NUS. Standard Double or Twin Room, S$287 for 3 nights + S$63 taxes and fees = **≈S$350 total**. Guest score 7.0 (Good, 95 reviews). Best value of the three.\n2. **ibis budget Singapore West Coast** (Queenstown) — 1 km from NUS. Standard Double Room (no window), S$306 + S$61 taxes = **≈S$367 total**. Score 7.4 (Good, 498 reviews).\n3. **The Quay Hotel West Coast** (Queenstown) — 1 km from NUS. Superior Double Room (no window), S$359 (down from S$399) + S$71 taxes = **≈S$430 total**. Score 7.0 (Good, 192 reviews).\n\n**My pick: Fragrance Hotel – Ocean View** — it ties for closest (1 km, roughly a 12–15 minute walk to campus) and is the cheapest at about S$350 all-in, leaving plenty of headroom under S$500. If you'd rather have the better-reviewed property, ibis budget Singapore West Coast is only ~S$17 more for a 7.4 score.\n\nNote: everything else in Singapore is 5.8 km or farther from NUS (e.g. Orchard Rendezvous at 5.8 km for ~S$856 all-in, Hotel Mi Bencoolen at 8.2 km for ~S$485 all-in), so these three are genuinely the closest options. I haven't booked anything — tell me which one you want and I can open its room/rate page to reserve.",
